sequenceDiagram
autonumber
participant C as Caller
participant I as ItemSystemComponent
participant K as ItemSpecContainer
participant M as Item components
participant G as Owner GAS
participant A as AbilitySystemComponent
C->>I: GiveItem(item, level, out index)
alt stackable, and a slot has room
I->>K: ChangeStacks(+1), equipped effects refresh
else a new slot
I->>I: CanGiveItem, item.Generate(self, level)
Note over I: the ItemSpec registers the item's level under its AssetTag
I->>K: new ItemSpecContainer(spec, index)
K->>M: Given
end
I-->>C: OnItemGiven
C->>I: EquipItem(index or item)
I->>K: CanEquipItem, then Equip()
K->>K: IsEquipped = true
K->>G: ApplyCarrier(effect.Generate(ItemSpec, Source)) per GrantedEffect
K-->>C: OnItemEffectsApplied
K->>A: GiveAbility(ActiveAbility, item level, out slot), LentBy the slot
K-->>C: OnItemAbilityGranted
K->>G: Item.InitWorkers(Source): workers, OnHit, modifiers
K->>M: Equipped: SetBonus calls ForgeSets.Refresh, Aura gives its aura
K->>G: CompileGrantedTags()
K-->>C: OnItemEquipped
Note over C,A: Use: an activation of the lent ability that committed ends
A->>K: AbilitySpec.HearEnd, then the slot's HearUsed
K->>M: Used, UsesItemComponent counts, then takes a stack or removes the item
C->>I: ConsumeItemTask calls ConsumeItem(item, n)
I->>I: RemoveItem(item, n), from the last slot first
I-->>C: OnItemConsumed(item, used)
C->>I: UnequipItem(index or item)
I->>K: Unequip()
K->>A: RemoveAbilityAt(slot, ability), OnItemAbilityRevoked
K->>G: RemoveGameplayEffect(effect, ItemSpec), OnItemEffectsRemoved
K->>M: Item.RemoveWorkers, Unequipped
K->>G: CompileGrantedTags(), OnItemUnequipped
C->>I: RemoveItem(index)
I->>K: unequip it if equipped, take it off the shelf
K->>M: Removed
I-->>C: OnItemRemoved
